From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: dw9719: accept the DW9763

The Xiaomi Mi MIX's rear camera focus motor is a DW9763 (ID 0xf9). The
stock actuator library programs it with the DW9761 register map (control
0x02, mode 0x06 = 0x41, prescale 0x07 = 0x3c), so treat it as a DW9761;
the SAC mode and prescale come from the device tree.

Also power the chip down when its ID is unknown: the probe failure path
released the regulator while still enabled (WARNING in regulator_put()).

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@
 #define DW9719_INFO			CCI_REG8(0)
 #define DW9719_ID			0xF1
 #define DW9761_ID			0xF4
+/* DW9763: the DW9761 register map (Xiaomi Mi MIX rear camera) */
+#define DW9763_ID			0xF9
 
 #define DW9719_CONTROL			CCI_REG8(2)
 #define DW9719_STANDBY			0x00
@@ -160,6 +162,7 @@
 			dw9719->vcm_freq = DW9719_DEFAULT_VCM_FREQ;
 			break;
 		case DW9761_ID:
+		case DW9763_ID:
 			dw9719->model = DW9761;
 			dw9719->mode_low_bits = 0x01;
 			dw9719->sac_mode = DW9761_DEFAULT_SAC;
@@ -168,6 +171,7 @@
 		default:
 			dev_err(dw9719->dev,
 				"Error unknown device id 0x%02llx\n", val);
+			dw9719_power_down(dw9719);
 			return -ENXIO;
 		}
 
